      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 60-year-old man presented with acute chest pain and dyspnoea, which was caused by pericarditis secondary to a neo-oesophago-pericardial fistula after previous oesophagectomy for oesophageal cancer. The fistula presumably originated from a penetrating peptic ulcer."},
